    "subtitle": "Greater clarity and understanding for the way forward.",
    "image": "/images/services/Student Counselling.png",
    "content": "**COUPLE COUNSELLING **\n\nA relationship can be strong, yet still face situations that are difficult to understand or navigate.\n\nTwo individuals may care deeply for each other and still experience differences in expectations, communication, priorities, family circumstances, cultural backgrounds, lifestyle choices or their vision for the future. At times, the concern may arise within the relationship itself. At other times, the relationship may be perfectly cordial, but external circumstances may create uncertainty about the future together.\n\n**Couple Counselling provides a structured and neutral space to understand these concerns, examine them objectively and explore the best possible way forward.**\n\nThe objective is not to decide who is right or wrong. It is to understand the situation from both perspectives, bring out the material issues, examine their implications and help the couple consciously consider what may need to change, adjust, accept or be better understood.\n\n\n\n\n\n**What may bring a couple to counselling?**\n\nCouples may seek counselling for a wide range of situations, including:\n\n· Communication gaps or recurring disagreements;\n\n· Difficulty understanding each other's thoughts, expectations or behaviour;\n\n· Differences in values, priorities, lifestyle or personal choices;\n\n· Trust-related concerns or emotional distance;\n\n· Compatibility-related concerns;\n\n· Differences regarding family expectations or relationships;\n\n· Different cultural or social backgrounds;\n\n· Geographical differences or concerns arising from living in different locations;\n\n· Career or job-related circumstances affecting the relationship;\n\n· Concerns about the future of the relationship;\n\n· Difficulty managing an external situation over which the couple has limited control;\n\n· Differences in expectations about responsibilities and the future; or\n\n· Any other situation where the couple feels that a neutral and thoughtful conversation may help.\n\nSometimes, **there may not even be a serious conflict between the two individuals**. They may simply want to understand how a particular situation could affect their relationship and consider the options available to them.\n\n\n\n\n\n**How does Couple Counselling help?**\n\nThe Counsellor listens to the perspectives of both individuals and seeks to understand **what the actual concern is, where it originates and how it is affecting the relationship or their understanding of the future together.**\n\nThe discussion may consider:\n\n· What each individual understands and expects;\n\n· Areas of alignment as well as areas of difference;\n\n· The underlying factors contributing to the concern;\n\n· The circumstances surrounding the issue;\n\n· The implications of different possible approaches;\n\n· Individual responsibilities and areas requiring consideration;\n\n· Relevant social and cultural considerations;\n\n· What may reasonably be changed or adjusted and what may need to be accepted; and\n\n· Whether a practical middle-ground or mutually workable approach may be possible.\n\nThe Counsellor also brings the **Social Counselling values and conscious-thinking filters** into the discussion wherever relevant, so that the couple is able to consider the situation from a wider and more balanced perspective.\n\nThe Counsellor may challenge an assumption, expectation or thought process where necessary. The purpose is not to tell the couple what they want to hear, but to help them **understand the situation more clearly and consciously.**\n\n\n\n\n\n**What could be the outcome?**\n\nEvery situation is different. Depending upon the circumstances, the counselling may help the couple:\n\n· reconcile differences;\n\n· arrive at a mutually workable or middle-ground solution;\n\n· establish more appropriate priorities;\n\n· develop more realistic expectations;\n\n· understand the impact of their respective thoughts or behaviour;\n\n· identify areas where a thought process may need to be fine-tuned; or\n\n· simply gain greater clarity about how they should move forward.\n\n**The Counsellor does not decide on behalf of the couple.**\n\nThe role of Social Counselling is to bring the relevant aspects to the table, examine them objectively and help the individuals consciously determine the most appropriate way forward.\n\n\n\n\n\n**What Couple Counselling does not handle**\n\nCouple Counselling is intended for relationship-related understanding and constructive resolution. It does not undertake matters requiring specialist legal, medical, psychological or professional intervention.\n\nSocial Counselling does not handle:\n\n· **Legal disputes or legal advice;**\n\n· **Family disputes** requiring formal intervention or adjudication;\n\n· **Discrimination, harassment or workplace-related matters** requiring specialist intervention;\n\n· **Psychological or psychiatric conditions** requiring clinical assessment or treatment; and\n\n· **Financial disputes, financial advice or matters requiring professional financial intervention.**\n\nWhere appropriate, individuals may be advised to seek suitable professional assistance.\n\n\n\n\n\n**Eligibility for Couple Counselling**\n\n· Applicable to couples whose relationship has **legal status in India**.\n\n· Both individuals must be **21 years of age or above**, as per Social Counselling policy.\n\n\n\n\n\n**Target Outcome\\***\n\n**To bring greater clarity and understanding into the relationship by identifying the genuine areas of concern, understanding related perspectives, examining the relevant circumstances and implications, and enabling the couple to consciously determine the most appropriate way forward.**\n\nThe outcome may involve reconciliation, adjustment, acceptance, changed expectations, better understanding or another mutually appropriate way forward, depending upon the circumstances.\n\n\\*Attention is drawn to the Client T&Cs and it is expressly communicated that Social Counselling cannot guarantee any particular outcome post counselling due to multiple external factors not within the control of Social Counselling. Please refer to the Client T&Cs for more details. Target outcome gets fine-tuned for each individual case."
